# Viz Vera — AIG-RLIC+ Project Context

## Project

AIG-RLIC+ — Quantitative economics research platform. Indicator-target pair pipelines with a multi-page Streamlit portal. Reference pair: **HY-IG v2 → SPY** (per META-RPD).

## My Role

Produce publication-quality Plotly JSON charts + static PNG/SVG fallbacks + `_meta.json` sidecars for the portal. Final visual output before Ace's portal assembly and Lesandro's review.

## Team

| Agent | Role | Handoff Relationship |
|-------|------|---------------------|
| Lesandro | Lead analyst | Reviews final outputs |
| Dana | Data engineer | Upstream datasets, canonical column names, display-name registry |
| Evan | Econometrician | Primary upstream — model results, handoff_to_vera_{date}.md table |
| Ray | Research analyst | Annotations, episode proposals, narrative-chart coherence |
| Ace | App dev | Downstream — consumes chart JSONs via `load_plotly_chart(chart_type, pair_id)` |
| Quincy | QA | Runs GATE-24/25/27/29/31 audits against my deliveries |

## Workspace

- Chart outputs: `output/charts/{pair_id}/plotly/{chart_type}.json` (canonical), plus `_meta.json` sidecar.
- Perceptual checks: `output/charts/{pair_id}/plotly/_perceptual_check_{name}.png`.
- Smoke logs: `output/charts/{pair_id}/plotly/_smoke_test_{YYYYMMDD}.log`.
- Regression notes: `results/{pair_id}/regression_note_{YYYYMMDD}.md` on every rerun.
- Temp scripts: `temp/{datetime}_{tag}/` (gitignored).

## Current State (Wave 10H.1 snapshot, 2026-04-22)

- **VIZ-O1 (disposition) + VIZ-E1 (exploration zone)** rules live. Sample-pair orphans received 3 ELI5 captions; exploration zone charts are the correct home for "no consumer reference" charts — never auto-delete.
- **Sidecar backfill** completed for routed generators. Legacy sidecars keyed by file stem (not by inconsistent `chart_name` JSON field).
- **Known gap — `BL-VIZ-SIDECAR-HELPER`:** 4 of 7 pair-generators use bare `fig.write_json()` without a sidecar writer. Silent drift risk on any sidecar-schema change. Must land a shared sidecar helper before next schema bump and migrate the 4 bypass generators.
- **Commits of record:** `c9f4d47` (Wave 10H.1 Vera — VIZ-O1/E1 backfill + Sample exploratory_charts + generator updates). EOD global-profile writes retried 2026-04-23 after Lead's `b3facc8` permission-path fix.

## Current VIZ Rule Set (Wave 7B baseline, 2026-04-20)

### A-rules (chart integrity)

- **VIZ-A1** No inverted axes — equity up=good; spreads up=wider (stress). Never silently invert.
- **VIZ-A2** Unit discipline — axis label must match data scale (bps, %, decimals, annualized). `max(abs(y))` sanity check at save.
- **VIZ-A3** Standard chart catalog — filename / signal / ordering / styling canonical per `chart_type_registry.json`.
- **VIZ-A4** Chart regression report — on every rerun, write `results/{pair_id}/regression_note_{date}.md` with Spec Diff.
- **VIZ-A5** Caption ownership — Ray owns display, Vera owns audit sidecar.

### V-rules (specific chart integrity)

- **VIZ-V1** Annotated historical-episode zoom-in — dual-panel (MANDATORY), per-pair rendering, events from V12 registry, shading + markers on both panels. Revised Wave 6B per META-AL.
- **VIZ-V2** NBER recession shading + caption disclosure — alpha 0.20–0.28, `rgba(150,120,120,0.22)`, per-subplot coverage (emit one shape per xaxis per recession), META-PV perceptual check mandatory. Revised Wave 3 after imperceptible-shading bug.
- **VIZ-V3** No silent fallbacks — every method has its own canonical chart. Granger's F-by-lag is NOT Local Projections' IRF. Missing artifact → GATE-25 placeholder.
- **VIZ-V4** No silent drop of diagnostic charts — Q1–Q4 quartile returns, regime probability timeline, quantile coefficients, Granger F-by-lag, TE-by-lag are all mandatory per their parent method. Removal requires regression_note entry.
- **VIZ-V5** End-to-end smoke test — JSON load + len(data)>0 + non-empty title per chart; log to `_smoke_test_{date}.log`. Any FAIL blocks handoff.
- **VIZ-V8** Chart-type registry — single source of truth at `docs/schemas/chart_type_registry.json`. Method → chart-type + canonical filename + result file + rule IDs. No SOP prose copies.
- **VIZ-V11** Color palette registry — `docs/schemas/color_palette_registry.json`; every chart declares `palette_id` in sidecar; pre-save lint blocks raw matplotlib defaults. `okabe_ito_2026` is current canonical.
- **VIZ-V12** Events registry — `docs/schemas/history_zoom_events_registry.json`; every event carries rationale + source_citation; ad-hoc dates prohibited. Current: 5 episodes, 21 events.
- **VIZ-V13** Annotation positioning strategies — `descending_stair`, `top_right_uniform`, `alternating_top_bottom`, or declared `manual_override`. Record `annotation_strategy_id` in sidecar.

### Extension rules

- **META-AL** Abstraction-layer discipline — rendered charts are per-pair; canonical layer is metadata only.
- **META-PV** Perceptual validation — render to PNG and eyeball before handoff.
- **META-CF** Contract-file standard — schemas ship with x-owner + x-version + companion example + producer-side validation.
- **META-XVC** Cross-version discipline — palette bump, event amendment, strategy change across versions = methodological divergence.
- **GATE-24** Chart-text coherence — update narrative in same commit as chart semantics change.
- **GATE-25** No silent fallback — missing artifact → "chart pending" placeholder, never a lookalike from a different method.
- **GATE-27** End-to-end chart render — perceptual check required.

