## Wave 10J Lessons (2026-04-24)

### Pattern: NBER shading without a mandatory chart-type list produces drift
Rule V2 said "long-horizon charts must have NBER shading" but without an explicit mandatory list, individual judgment at chart-creation time produced 5/10 hero charts missing shading and all rolling charts unshaded. VIZ-NBER1 now provides the explicit list — follow it mechanically, not by judgment.

### Pattern: Missing trigger rule for zoom charts causes inconsistency
8/10 pairs had zero zoom charts because no rule defined when they were required. VIZ-ZOOM1 now provides the three-condition trigger (data coverage + domain relevance + portal delivery). Apply it at pair-creation time, not after the fact.

### Pattern: CP chart types need canonical specs before Evan delivers
When ECON-CP1/CP2 results arrive, Vera needs VIZ-CP1 specs already in the SOP — not ad-hoc decisions at delivery time. VIZ-CP1 now covers all five chart types with NBER shading requirements and layout specs.

## 2026-04-24 — Wave 10J/10K Self-Reflection

### What went well
- Debate contributions were evidence-grounded: live role-boundary violation in VIZ-NBER1, shared-script gap in ECON-DIR1/RES-OD1, direction-vocabulary seam — all cited with rule IDs and wave references.
- Self-assessment produced accurate defect mapping before being prompted: 5 hero charts missing NBER, 9 other mandatory charts missing, 34 zoom charts missing across 8 pairs.
- Canonical contract architecture (VIZ-V8/V12/V13) held across 10 pairs — zero undocumented annotation strategies or off-palette colors.

### NBER shading gap root cause
Rule V2 existed since Wave 3, but pair pipeline scripts were forked from a pre-Wave 3 original. Hand-crafted charts (HY-IG) were compliant; pipeline-generated charts were not. Treated "rule exists in SOP" as equivalent to "rule is implemented in all code paths." Those are not the same thing. Fix: VIZ-V2 must be enforced at generation time in the chart helper function, not post-hoc via audit.

### Role boundary violation root cause
Only caught VIZ-NBER1 prescribing Quincy's verification method because the debate format forced reading own SOP as external reviewer. Normal production dispatches don't create that perspective — which means violations persist indefinitely without structured review.

### Perceptual PNG carry-forward
Three compounding failures: kaleido 0.2.x WARNs treated as cosmetic; no blocking downstream gate; deferred as "separate track" without assigning an agent or wave. Will not close until Ace upgrades kaleido and Quincy adds PNG existence to GATE-27.

### Walk-forward redesign debate
Redesign with continuous datetime axes is architecturally correct but blocked on Evan's fold-level oos_start_date/oos_end_date output. Track as cross-agent dependency on Evan, not a Vera backlog item.

### Key lessons to carry forward
1. "Rule exists in SOP" ≠ "rule is implemented in all code paths." Audit pipeline scripts at rule-authoring time.
2. Blocking gates must live in production code, not in memory or SOP text.
3. Kaleido deprecation warnings on mandatory checks are compliance gaps, not cosmetic issues.

## 2026-06-12 — Plotly fill-band traces silently render default-palette markers

A `go.Scatter` CI-band trace (`fill="toself"`, `line=dict(width=0)`) without an explicit `mode="lines"` renders markers at every band vertex in Plotly's default cycle colors (purple/teal). The palette-conformance lint cannot catch it because `marker.color` is None — the color is resolved at render time. Two charts (local_projections, quantile_coef) shipped through VIZ-IC1 clean and were caught only by the perceptual-PNG eyeball.

**How to apply:** always set `mode="lines"` on fill-band traces; treat "lint passed but render-time defaults exist" as a known blind spot the perceptual check covers.
- Smoke tests: hy_ig_v2_spy 15/0, indpro_xlp 8/0, umcsent_xlv 7/0. All pass.
- Commit: 3c6bb50 (65 files, +516/-34)

**Key lesson:** Filename migration is never just `git mv`. Consumer call sites must be updated atomically in the same commit. Smoke test catches mismatches immediately.

**wc -l evidence (before → after):** experience.md 79→93 (+14), memories.md 70→103 (+33).

