 A `go.Scatter` CI-band trace (`fill="toself"`, `line=dict(width=0)`) without an explicit `mode="lines"` renders markers at every band vertex in Plotly's default cycle colors (purple/teal). The palette-conformance lint cannot catch it because `marker.color` is None — the color is resolved at render time. Two charts (local_projections, quantile_coef) shipped through VIZ-IC1 clean and were caught only by the perceptual-PNG eyeball.
 
 **How to apply:** always set `mode="lines"` on fill-band traces; treat "lint passed but render-time defaults exist" as a known blind spot the perceptual check covers.
